==Requirement Strategies==
*For the first requirement, focus on picking up [[Research Capsules]] and extracting [[Machines]]. The Machine and Capsule count increases the further you descend, so you can earn more {{II|Ichor|name=true}}.
*For the second requirement, just get close to {{CI|Twisted Connie|name=true}} if she's on a [[Floor]] so you can get her Research. Playing as {{CI|Rodger|name=true}} also helps to get Research faster because of his Passive [[Ability]], '''Detective'''. This will be easier if Twisted Connie is on the [[Daily Twisted Board]].

==Strategies==
Connie could be considered the best survivalist [[Toon]] in the game, having the highest [[Stealth]] in the game alongside an [[Ability]] that's quite helpful against escaping dangerous [[Twisteds]]. She also has above average [[Extraction Speed]], making her great for those who want to extract more efficiently. However, Connie possesses low mobility [[Statistics]], that being 1{{Star}} [[Movement Speed]] and an average [[Stamina]] capacity, along with below average [[Skill Check]], needing some skill to play her safely.

Connie's lowest Stat, being Movement Speed, is something that should be mitigated in a way or another, as by herself, she cannot outrun most Twisteds in the game. For that reason alone, keeping Movement Speed [[Items]] like {{II|Box o' Chocolates|name=false|plural=a}} or {{II|Speed Candy|name=false|plural=a}} in your inventory, using [[Trinkets]] such as {{TI|Pink Bow|name=true}}, and getting speed boosts from support Toons is a few of the the things you could do in order to make her better to move around more easily.

Focusing on her main Ability, {{AI|Connie|name=true}}, one can see it's potential in helping the player out of sticky situations, such as being chased by a Twisted that Connie can't out-run (eg. {{CI|Twisted Shelly|name=true}} or {{CI|Twisted Toodles|name=true}}). Her Ability is, in a way, an infinite source of {{II|Smoke Bomb|name=false|plural=a}}, having a somewhat short cooldown with a short duration. Though great on the surface, some issues may arise from it, as it does not work on [[:Category:Ranged Twisteds|Ranged]] or {{Type|Lethal}} Twisteds, so instead of using her Ability on them, hiding or avoiding being seen by any of those in the aforementioned categories can save you a life.

However, Connie is more than her Ability. In addition to having the highest Stealth in the game, she has immunity to [[Ichor Leaks]] and produces light during [[Blackouts]], making her even better for wandering around as well as surviving during [[Floor Events]]. On top of those, her good extractability makes her great for extracting Machines that are near distractors and other Machines that are in dangerous spots, so long as you don't miss a Skill Check or more, given that the Stat is subpar. Her Ichor Puddle Immunity in general is also useful when it comes to {{CI|Twisted Finn|name=true}} and {{CI|Twisted Tisha|name=true}} (situationally), as their special abilities can make traversal or extraction more difficult due to the [[Debuffs]]. {{Debuff|Illness}} would normally be an issue, especially with Connie's 2 Star Skill Check, but she can't be affected by the -50% size decrease, and thus no worry of an involuntary, significant size decrease. 

Despite all of the upsides mentioned above, Connie is less than adequate for completing [[Dyle's Floor]], because, as aforementioned, her Ability doesn't work on {{CI|Twisted Dyle|name=true}}, and nor does she have a chance at escaping him if in his line of sight for too long. While completing his Floor as her is not impossible, it's definitely a hard task, and there are better options out there if you wish to complete his Floor with ease. Even if you somehow escape, her increased Stamina can't be utilized to the max, as although she can sprint more, she can't sprint faster, so running away from faster Twisteds is still harder.

Overall, Connie is a great survivalist and decent extractor, yet struggles with mobility, which can be somewhat alleviated in one way or another.

